  Kompakt power profile. Mudita's vendor ships AOSP's placeholder (two made-up CPU
  clusters, 0.1 mA everywhere, a 1000 mAh battery), so Android computed no drain
  and Battery usage stayed empty. Sources:

  CPU, memory, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, GPS and modem: the Infinix X626 (same MT6761, an
  identical 4-core cluster with the same 16 speeds, 850 MHz to 2.001 GHz) stock
  profile, vendor/hardware_overlay/Infinix/S4, measured by that phone's maker.

  Screen and sleep: this phone's own fuel gauge, 2026-10-10, unplugged, airplane
  mode with Wi-Fi (adb): screen on and still 121 mA at minimum light, 141 mA at
  full light, 232 mA while the panel repaints continuously; asleep 3 to 4 mA from
  the coulomb counter over 18 minutes. An e-ink panel draws nothing between
  refreshes, so screen.on is small and the awake SoC carries the rest.

  battery.capacity: what this phone charges the cell to, 3037 mAh at 4.34 V (Mudita's
  gauge table); the label, LS061A, rates it 3300 mAh at 4.45 V.
-->
